add_message_at_rest_encryption.s:
"In transit" is already satisfied today with zero code changes needed: every client<->Worker request is Cloudflare-terminated TLS (HTTPS for /api/send, WSS for the ws/ realtime relay) — confirmed via fork audit that no other transport is used. Skip that half; state it, don't re-implement it.

"At rest" is fully greenfield: src/lib/server/chat.ts stores `payload.x` (message text) as plaintext in Qdrant (confirmed: send_msg/send_group_msg build `payload: m as unknown as Record<string, unknown>` with `x: text` raw, chat.ts:37-54 and :70-89). Add AES-256-GCM encryption of the `x` field specifically at the Qdrant-persistence boundary, decrypting transparently on every read path, so every caller of chat.ts (API routes, search) continues to see plaintext and needs no changes.

Create src/lib/server/msg_crypto.ts (new file):
```ts
import { get_secret, type QEnv, type SecretVal } from './qdrant';

let cached: CryptoKey | null = null;

async function aes_key(env: QEnv & { MESSAGE_ENC_KEY?: SecretVal }): Promise<CryptoKey> {
	if (cached) return cached;
	const raw = await get_secret(env.MESSAGE_ENC_KEY);
	const bytes = Uint8Array.from(atob(raw), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0));
	cached = await crypto.subtle.importKey('raw', bytes, 'AES-GCM', false, ['encrypt', 'decrypt']);
	return cached;
}

export async function encrypt_text(env: QEnv, text: string): Promise<string> {
	if (!text) return text;
	const key = await aes_key(env);
	const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
	const buf = await crypto.subtle.encrypt({ name: 'AES-GCM', iv }, key, new TextEncoder().encode(text));
	const combined = new Uint8Array(iv.length + buf.byteLength);
	combined.set(iv, 0);
	combined.set(new Uint8Array(buf), iv.length);
	return 'enc:' + btoa(String.fromCharCode(...combined));
}

// ponytail: legacy plaintext messages (stored before this change) have no 'enc:' prefix and
// are returned as-is — no backfill migration. Run one if full at-rest coverage of pre-existing
// messages is required.
export async function decrypt_text(env: QEnv, stored: string): Promise<string> {
	if (!stored.startsWith('enc:')) return stored;
	try {
		const combined = Uint8Array.from(atob(stored.slice(4)), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0));
		const key = await aes_key(env);
		const buf = await crypto.subtle.decrypt(
			{ name: 'AES-GCM', iv: combined.slice(0, 12) },
			key,
			combined.slice(12)
		);
		return new TextDecoder().decode(buf);
	} catch {
		return stored;
	}
}
```
`cached` module-level `CryptoKey` mirrors the existing `q`/`q_key` module-level caching pattern already used in qdrant.ts:23-26 for the Qdrant client — same lazy-singleton idiom, same file's convention.

In src/lib/server/chat.ts: add `import { encrypt_text, decrypt_text } from './msg_crypto';` after line 4 (`import { get_group } from './group';`). In `send_msg` (lines 28-56), change the payload build so only the *stored* copy is encrypted, keeping the returned `m` (used for the API response, the WS relay text, and `backfill_vector`'s plaintext embedding input) untouched:
```ts
export async function send_msg(
	env: QEnv,
	from: string,
	to: string,
	text: string,
	image?: string,
	file?: Message['fl']
): Promise<Message> {
	await ensure(env);
	const m: Message = {
		s: 'm',
		id: new_id(),
		c: conv_id(from, to),
		f: from,
		t: to,
		x: text,
		...(image ? { im: image } : {}),
		...(file ? { fl: file } : {}),
		d: Date.now()
	};
	await upsert(env, [
		{
			id: m.id,
			vector: {},
			payload: { ...m, x: await encrypt_text(env, text) } as unknown as Record<string, unknown>
		}
	]);
	return m;
}
```
Apply the identical `payload: { ...m, x: await encrypt_text(env, text) }` change to `send_group_msg` (lines 61-90, same shape). This is safe for `backfill_vector` (chat.ts:21-26, called separately by the API route with the original plaintext `text` variable, never re-reading from Qdrant) — the embedding pipeline is unaffected.

Decrypt on every read path — `page_msgs` (chat.ts:110-117), used by both `get_messages` and `get_group_messages`:
```ts
async function page_msgs(env: QEnv, conv: string, before?: number): Promise<Message[]> {
	const pts = await scroll(env, f(eq('s', 'm'), eq('c', conv)), PAGE, undefined, {
		key: 'd',
		direction: 'desc',
		...(before === undefined ? {} : { start_from: before - 1 })
	});
	const msgs = await Promise.all(
		pts.map(async (p) => {
			const m = p.payload as unknown as Message;
			return { ...m, x: await decrypt_text(env, m.x) };
		})
	);
	return msgs.sort((x, y) => x.d - y.d);
}
```
`search_messages` (chat.ts:92-106), decrypt the mapped result:
```ts
export async function search_messages(
	env: QEnv,
	uid: string,
	q: string,
	conv?: string,
	limit = 20
): Promise<Message[]> {
	await ensure(env);
	const vector = await embed(env, q);
	const filter = conv
		? f(eq('s', 'm'), eq('c', conv))
		: f_or([eq('s', 'm')], [eq('f', uid), eq('t', uid)]);
	const pts = await search(env, vector, filter, limit);
	return Promise.all(
		pts.map(async (p) => {
			const m = p.payload as unknown as Message;
			return { ...m, x: await decrypt_text(env, m.x) };
		})
	);
}
```
`edit_msg` (chat.ts:138-158) — decrypt the retrieved text before using it to build `next`, and encrypt the new text on the way back in; the *returned* `next` (used by the caller for the WS 'edit' relay body) must stay plaintext:
```ts
export async function edit_msg(
	env: QEnv,
	uid: string,
	msg_id: string,
	new_text: string
): Promise<Message> {
	await ensure(env);
	const pt = await retrieve_one(env, msg_id, true);
	if (!pt || pt.payload?.s !== 'm') throw new Error('not found');
	const m = pt.payload as unknown as Message;
	if (m.f !== uid) throw new Error('not author');
	const next = { ...m, x: new_text, e: Date.now() };
	await upsert(env, [
		{
			id: msg_id,
			vector: pt.vector ?? {},
			payload: { ...next, x: await encrypt_text(env, new_text) } as unknown as Record<string, unknown>
		}
	]);
	return next;
}
```
(`delete_msg`, chat.ts:160-176, needs no change — it never reads or returns `.x`.)

Deploy-time step (not code, but required for this to function; note it explicitly rather than leaving it implicit): generate a 256-bit key with `openssl rand -base64 32`, provision it as a Secrets Store secret named `MESSAGE_ENC_KEY` following the repo's existing convention (CLAUDE.md: `wrangler secrets-store secret create <store_id> --name MESSAGE_ENC_KEY --scopes workers` for local dev; add `{ binding: "MESSAGE_ENC_KEY", store_id, secret_name: "MESSAGE_ENC_KEY" }` to `secrets_store_secrets` in wrangler.jsonc for production, alongside the existing entries for QDRANT_URL/VOXELL_KEY/etc). `QEnv` (qdrant.ts:57-65) needs `MESSAGE_ENC_KEY?: SecretVal` added to its type so `env.MESSAGE_ENC_KEY` typechecks in msg_crypto.ts without a cast.

Why AES-GCM via Web Crypto over a library: `crypto.subtle` is a Workers-native global (already used identically in push.ts for Web Push payload encryption) — zero new dependency, authenticated encryption (GCM tag prevents tampering), matches ladder rung 4 (native platform feature).

