add_sqids_group_ids.s:
Currently every group/room id is `crypto.randomUUID()` via the shared `new_id()` in src/lib/server/qdrant.ts:76 (`export const new_id = (): string => crypto.randomUUID();`), called from `save_group` (group.ts:83, `id: new_id()`). `new_id()` is shared — messages (chat.ts:39,72) and other entities call it too, so it must not change; add a dedicated id generator for groups only.

Add dependency: `pnpm add sqids`.

In src/lib/server/qdrant.ts, add after the existing `new_id` export (line 76):
```ts
import Sqids from 'sqids';

const sqids = new Sqids({ minLength: 9 });

// 9+ char room id: two 32-bit random numbers give ~62 bits of entropy, matching the
// existing `available_username`-style collision-retry convention (username.ts) rather than
// assuming zero collisions.
export async function new_group_id(env: QEnv, exists: (id: string) => Promise<boolean>): Promise<string> {
	for (let tries = 0; tries < 5; tries += 1) {
		const rnd = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(2));
		const id = sqids.encode([rnd[0], rnd[1]]);
		if (!(await exists(id))) return id;
	}
	throw new Error('id_unavailable');
}
```
Move the `import Sqids from 'sqids';` to the top of the file with the other imports (qdrant.ts:1, alongside `import { QdrantClient } from '@qdrant/js-client-rest';`) rather than inline — inline shown above only to mark placement relative to `new_id`.

In src/lib/server/group.ts: add `new_group_id` to the import from `./qdrant` (line 1-14 import block, alongside the existing `new_id` import — keep `new_id` too, it's unused by group.ts after this change so remove it from the import list since nothing else in this file calls it — confirm via grep `new_id(` in group.ts returns only the one call site being replaced). Replace `save_group` (group.ts:72-96) line 83 `id: new_id(),` with:
```ts
		id: await new_group_id(env, async (id) => (await retrieve_one(env, id)) !== null),
```
`retrieve_one` is already imported in group.ts (line 6). This mirrors `available_username`'s exact retry-loop idiom (src/lib/server/username.ts) already established in this codebase for id-uniqueness — same pattern, different entity, per repo convention of reusing existing idioms rather than inventing a new one.

No migration needed for existing groups — ids are opaque strings everywhere (Group.id: string, GroupView.id: string, routes use `[id]` params, mb/ow references are also plain uid strings unrelated to this) — old UUID-format room ids keep working unchanged; only newly-created rooms get 9+ char sqids.

Why sqids over nanoid/shorter uuid: explicitly requested by name; `minLength: 9` is the library's own mechanism for enforcing the length floor (pads short encodes, never truncates long ones) rather than hand-rolling truncation, which would reduce entropy unpredictably.

Test: create src/lib/server/__tests__/group_id.test.ts:
```ts
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import { new_group_id } from '../qdrant';

describe('new_group_id', () => {
	it('returns an id at least 9 characters long', async () => {
		const id = await new_group_id({} as never, async () => false);
		expect(id.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(9);
	});
	it('retries when the generated id already exists, then succeeds', async () => {
		let calls = 0;
		const exists = vi.fn(async () => {
			calls += 1;
			return calls === 1; // first id "taken", second is free
		});
		const id = await new_group_id({} as never, exists);
		expect(exists).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
		expect(id.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(9);
	});
	it('throws after 5 failed attempts', async () => {
		await expect(new_group_id({} as never, async () => true)).rejects.toThrow('id_unavailable');
	});
});
```
