add_room_tags_field.s:
Mirror the exact pattern User interests already use (types.ts:13 `i?: string[]`, folded into the embed text in profile.ts) onto Group, using a different payload key: `tg` is already taken (mute.ts's mute-target field, indexed in qdrant.ts's KEYWORD_KEYS), so room tags use `tgs`. Interests (`i`) are deliberately NOT in KEYWORD_KEYS (qdrant.ts:98-100 list has no `i`) — they only feed the embedding, no exact-match filtering exists for them. Mirror that exactly: `tgs` is not added to KEYWORD_KEYS either, keeping room tags and user interests symmetric.

In src/lib/server/group.ts: add `tg` — no, add `tgs?: string[]; // tags (tokens), folds into the room's embedding like a user's interests` to the `Group` interface (group.ts:18-29), after line 22 (`ds: string; // description`):
```ts
export interface Group {
	s: 'g';
	id: string;
	nm: string; // name
	ds: string; // description
	tgs?: string[]; // tags (tokens), folds into the room's embedding like a user's interests
	ow: string; // owner uid
	mb: string[]; // member uids (owner included)
	d: number; // created ts
	co?: string; // country
	st?: string; // state / province
	ci?: string; // city
}
```
Add `tags?: string[];` to `GroupView` (group.ts:31-42) after `description: string;`, and in the `view()` function (group.ts:44-55) add `...(g.tgs?.length ? { tags: g.tgs } : {}),` after the `description: g.ds,` line.

Extend `group_text` (group.ts:58-59) to include tags in the embedding, mirroring profile.ts's `interests.length ? 'user_interests: ...' : ''` pattern:
```ts
const group_text = (name: string, description: string, tags?: string[]) =>
	`group_name: ${name}${description.trim() ? ` | group_about: ${description}` : ''}${tags?.length ? ` | room_tags: ${tags.join(', ')}` : ''}`;
```
Update its two call sites: `put()` (group.ts:61-66) `group_text(g.nm, g.ds)` → `group_text(g.nm, g.ds, g.tgs)`; `update_group`'s changed-check (group.ts:136) `group_text(next.nm, next.ds) !== group_text(cur.nm, cur.ds)` → `group_text(next.nm, next.ds, next.tgs) !== group_text(cur.nm, cur.ds, cur.tgs)`.

Thread `tags` through `save_group` (group.ts:72-96): add `tags?: string[]` to the `data` param type (line 76), and in the built `Group` object (lines 81-92) add `...(data.tags?.length ? { tgs: data.tags } : {}),` after the `ds:` line.

Thread it through `update_group` (group.ts:121-139): add `tags?: string[]` to the `updates` param type (line 125), and in the `next: Group` build (lines 130-135) add `...(updates.tags !== undefined ? { tgs: updates.tags } : {}),` after the `ds:` line.

In src/routes/api/groups/+server.ts and src/routes/api/groups/[id]/+server.ts (the POST-create and PATCH-update handlers that call `save_group`/`update_group` — read these two files first to find their exact request-body destructuring, matching the existing `name`/`description`/`country`/`state`/`city` pattern) add `tags` to the destructured body and pass it through to `save_group(env, ws, uid, { ..., tags })` / `update_group(env, id, uid, { ..., tags })`.

UI — mirror src/routes/app/profile/+page.svelte's exact interests-token block (lines 102-110 for the two handler functions, lines 150-176 for the markup) into the room create modal (src/routes/app/rooms/+page.svelte). Add state after line 28 (`let description = $state('');`):
```js
	let tags = $state<string[]>([]);
	let tagInput = $state('');
	function addTag() {
		const t = tagInput.trim();
		if (t && !tags.includes(t)) tags = [...tags, t];
		tagInput = '';
	}
	function removeTag(t: string) {
		tags = tags.filter((x) => x !== t);
	}
```
Insert the token-field markup into the create-room `<Modal>` form (rooms/+page.svelte:198-216), right after the `<textarea>` (line 204) and before `<LocationPicker>` (line 205):
```svelte
			<div class="flex min-h-[48px] flex-wrap items-center gap-2 rounded-[12px] border border-line bg-panel-solid px-3 py-2 transition-colors duration-300 focus-within:border-accent">
				{#each tags as t}
					<span class="flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full border border-line bg-panel px-3 py-1 text-[13px] text-ink">
						{t}
						<button type="button" onclick={() => removeTag(t)} class="text-[15px] leading-none text-faint transition-colors hover:text-accent" aria-label="remove {t}">&times;</button>
					</span>
				{/each}
				<input
					class="min-w-[100px] flex-1 border-none bg-transparent px-1 py-1 text-[14px] text-ink outline-none placeholder:text-mute"
					bind:value={tagInput}
					onkeydown={(e) => { if (e.key === 'Enter') (e.preventDefault(), addTag()); }}
					placeholder={tags.length ? '' : 'add a tag…'}
				/>
			</div>
```
Add `tags` to the `create()` fetch body (rooms/+page.svelte:68-72, alongside `name`/`description`/`country`/`state`/`city`).

This same token block + `tags`/`ename`-style state must also be added to the edit-room form once it becomes a modal in [[convert_room_crud_to_shallow_routed_modals]] — do not duplicate this sub-step there; that step references this one for the tags block markup.

Why mirror the interests pattern exactly rather than build a shared `<TagInput>` component: the ladder favors reuse of an existing pattern already proven in this codebase over introducing a new shared component for two call sites — if a third token-field use case appears later, extract then, not now (YAGNI on the abstraction, not on the feature).

