add_room_state_field.s:
No lifecycle/status concept exists on Group today (confirmed: grep for state/status/st in group.ts only finds `st` = geo state/province, group.ts:27, already used for `apply_location`). Add a genuinely new field — geographic `st` is taken, so room lifecycle state uses a new key `rs` (repo convention per AGENTS.md: stored enum values are single characters, mapped to full labels only for display).

Values: `a` = active (default, shows in search/list), `p` = paused (hidden from search results and the joined-rooms default view is unaffected — still visible to members, just not discoverable by new people), `c` = closed (same visibility rule as paused; distinguishes "temporarily quiet" from "permanently done" for the room's own members, display-only distinction, no different enforced behavior between p/c beyond both being excluded from discovery).

In src/lib/server/group.ts: add `rs: 'a' | 'p' | 'c'; // room state — a:active p:paused c:closed, default a` to the `Group` interface (group.ts:18-29) after the `mb` line. Add `state_r: 'a' | 'p' | 'c';` — no: reuse the word `state` is already GroupView's geo-state property name (group.ts:39 `state?: string;`), so the view-layer field must be named differently, e.g. `roomState`. Add `roomState: 'a' | 'p' | 'c';` to `GroupView` (group.ts:31-42) after `owner: string;`. In `view()` (group.ts:44-55) add `roomState: g.rs ?? 'a',` after `owner: g.ow,`.

In `save_group` (group.ts:72-96): add `state?: 'a' | 'p' | 'c'` to the `data` param type — this collides in naming with the already-present `data.state` (geo state/province, group.ts:76 `state?: string`)! Do not reuse that name. Name the new param `room_state?: 'a' | 'p' | 'c'` throughout (function param, API request body key, and client state variable) to keep it unambiguous from the existing geographic `state`. Build: `rs: data.room_state ?? 'a',` in the constructed `Group` object (after the `mb:` line).

In `update_group` (group.ts:121-139): add `room_state?: 'a' | 'p' | 'c'` to the `updates` param type, and in the `next: Group` build add `...(updates.room_state !== undefined ? { rs: updates.room_state } : {}),`. A room-state-only edit (no name/description change) should skip re-embedding exactly like a location-only edit does today — it already will, since `group_text` (touched in [[add_room_tags_field]]) never reads `rs`, so the existing `changed = group_text(...) !== group_text(...)` check in update_group naturally stays false and `put_payload` (the cheap path) is used.

Add `rs` to `KEYWORD_KEYS` in src/lib/server/qdrant.ts:99 (`'s', 't', 'r', 'c', 'f', 'co', 'st', 'ci', 'u', 'ow', 'mb', 'gr', 'uid', 'ac', 'tg', 'k'` → append `'rs'`) so it's filterable — unlike `tgs`, `rs` needs filtering because default room discovery must exclude paused/closed rooms (a field with zero query-time behavior isn't worth adding).

In `list_groups` (group.ts:172-176) and `search_groups`/`loc_filter` (group.ts:178-210): the default (unfiltered-by-uid) listing and search should exclude `rs !== 'a'` UNLESS `uid` is given (a member's own joined-rooms list, via `list_groups(env, uid)`, must show all their rooms regardless of state — only the public discovery path filters). Change `list_groups`:
```ts
export async function list_groups(env: QEnv, uid?: string, limit = 50): Promise<GroupView[]> {
	await ensure(env);
	const clauses = uid ? [eq('s', 'g'), eq('mb', uid)] : [eq('s', 'g'), eq('rs', 'a')];
	const pts = await scroll(env, f(...clauses), limit);
	return pts.map((p) => view(p.payload as unknown as Group)).sort((a, b) => b.created - a.created);
}
```
And `loc_filter` (group.ts:178-184), which backs `search_groups`'s public discovery path:
```ts
function loc_filter(loc: { country?: string; state?: string; city?: string }) {
	const clauses = [eq('s', 'g'), eq('rs', 'a')];
	if (loc.country) clauses.push(eq('co', loc.country));
	if (loc.state) clauses.push(eq('st', loc.state));
	if (loc.city) clauses.push(eq('ci', loc.city));
	return f(...clauses);
}
```
and the two `f(eq('s', 'g'))` fallback filters inside `search_groups` (group.ts:194, 202) that run when there's no location filter → change both to `f(eq('s', 'g'), eq('rs', 'a'))`.

Existing groups created before this migration have no `rs` field at all — Qdrant's `eq('rs', 'a')` filter would exclude them from discovery (a missing field never matches an `eq` clause), silently hiding every pre-existing room from search. This is the one place a light migration IS warranted (not skippable, unlike the encryption backfill) since it would otherwise break search for all current rooms on deploy. Handle it at the read layer instead of a write migration (simpler, no bulk-update script): change `eq('rs', 'a')` to instead exclude the two "away" states, treating absence as active — Qdrant doesn't support a "not equal" match directly via `eq`, so use `scroll`/`search`'s existing `filter` shape's `must_not` — check whether the `Cond`/`f()` filter helpers in qdrant.ts (lines 78-89) support `must_not` before assuming; if not, add it:
```ts
export const f_not = (musts: Cond[], nots: Cond[]) => ({ must: musts, must_not: nots });
```
in qdrant.ts alongside `f`/`f_or` (line 87-89), and use `f_not([eq('s', 'g')], [eq('rs', 'p'), eq('rs', 'c')])` in place of `f(eq('s', 'g'), eq('rs', 'a'))` everywhere above — this correctly treats both "no rs field" (legacy rooms) and "rs: 'a'" as discoverable, only actively excluding `p`/`c`.

