No endpoint exists to fetch a single message by id outside its own conversation's paginated window — confirmed: `src/routes/api/messages/[id]/edit/+server.ts` and `.../delete/+server.ts` exist as separate action routes, but `src/routes/api/messages/[id]/+server.ts` itself (a plain GET) does not. This is needed by [[add_message_reply_quote]] (resolving a quoted message that has scrolled out of the loaded window) and [[add_reply_privately_from_room]] (quoting a room message from inside a different 1:1 conversation entirely, which never shares a loaded `messages` array with the target chat).

Create src/routes/api/messages/[id]/+server.ts (new file):
```ts
import { json, error } from '@sveltejs/kit';
import type { RequestHandler } from './$types';
import { env } from '$env/dynamic/private';
import { get_message } from '$lib/server/chat';
import { is_member } from '$lib/server/group';

export const GET: RequestHandler = async ({ params, locals }) => {
	if (!locals.user) throw error(401, 'auth');
	const m = await get_message(env, params.id);
	if (!m) throw error(404, 'not found');
	const uid = locals.user.id;
	const allowed = m.gr
		? await is_member(env, locals.x2_ws, m.gr, uid)
		: m.f === uid || m.t === uid;
	if (!allowed) throw error(403, 'not a participant');
	return json({ m });
};
```
Add `get_message` to src/lib/server/chat.ts (new export, placed after `page_msgs` around line 117, reusing the same decrypt treatment from [[add_message_at_rest_encryption]]):
```ts
export async function get_message(env: QEnv, id: string): Promise<Message | null> {
	const pt = await retrieve_one(env, id);
	if (!pt || pt.payload?.s !== 'm') return null;
	const m = pt.payload as unknown as Message;
	return { ...m, x: await decrypt_text(env, m.x) };
}
```
`retrieve_one` is already imported in chat.ts (line 2). This step depends on [[add_message_at_rest_encryption]] having already added the `decrypt_text` import to chat.ts — if that step hasn't landed yet when this one is executed, add `import { decrypt_text } from './msg_crypto';` here instead (idempotent either way, same import).

Authorization mirrors the existing pattern used by group.ts's `is_member` (already used for join/leave/message-send gating) for group messages, and a direct `f`/`t` uid match for 1:1 — no new authorization primitive invented.

