The "user similarity" feature the request refers to is `whats_in_common()` in src/lib/server/groq.ts, surfaced via `findCommon()` in src/routes/app/user/[id]/+page.svelte and its backing route src/routes/api/user/[id]/common/+server.ts — it is NOT vector similarity search (no "similar"/"similarity" string exists anywhere in the codebase; confirmed by full-repo grep), it's an LLM one-liner ("what do these two people have in common") currently powered by Groq (`api.groq.com`, model from `pricing.ts`'s `GROQ_MODEL`), a third AI provider distinct from both Modal.dev (AI chat) and Voxell (embeddings). Migrate it onto Modal.dev, consolidating to the same provider/model already pinned in [[pin_ai_chat_model]], both to satisfy the explicit request and to reduce the feature's failure surface to one fewer external dependency.

`modal_stream` (modal.ts) is SSE-streaming-only, unsuited to a single-shot "give me one sentence" call — add a non-streaming sibling rather than forcing the streaming client through a stream-to-string wrapper (ladder: match the shape of what's actually needed, don't force-fit the existing function). In src/lib/server/modal.ts, add after `modal_stream` (line 59):
```ts
export async function modal_complete(
	env: QEnv & { MODAL_ENDPOINT_URL?: SecretVal; MODAL_WORKSPACE?: SecretVal; MODAL_ENDPOINT_NAME?: SecretVal; MODAL_ROUTING_REGION?: SecretVal; MODAL_PROXY_TOKEN_ID?: SecretVal; MODAL_PROXY_TOKEN_SECRET?: SecretVal },
	messages: { role: string; content: string }[]
): Promise<string> {
	const url = await endpoint(env);
	const auth = await auth_header(env);
	const controller = new AbortController();
	const timeout = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 20_000);
	try {
		const res = await fetch(`${url}/v1/chat/completions`, {
			method: 'POST',
			headers: { Authorization: auth, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
			body: JSON.stringify({ model: 'gemma-4-26b-a4b-it', messages, stream: false }),
			signal: controller.signal
		});
		if (!res.ok) throw new Error('modal_error');
		const data = (await res.json()) as { choices: { message: { content: string } }[] };
		const text = data.choices[0]?.message?.content?.trim();
		if (!text) throw new Error('modal_empty');
		return text;
	} finally {
		clearTimeout(timeout);
	}
}
```
The 20s `AbortController` timeout directly serves "never fails" — today's `whats_in_common` has no timeout at all, so a hung upstream request would hang the whole feature indefinitely rather than failing gracefully into the existing credit-refund path; this closes that gap.

Rewrite `whats_in_common` in src/lib/server/groq.ts (rename the file's export usage stays the same — keep the function name and its call sites in the route unchanged, only its internal implementation changes, so `src/routes/api/user/[id]/common/+server.ts` needs zero edits):
```ts
import { deduct, credit } from './credit_client';
import { modal_complete } from './modal';
import type { QEnv } from './qdrant';
import type { User } from '../types';

const ESTIMATE_KOBO = 500; // flat, small — one short sentence, no per-token pricing available for this provider

function profile_summary(u: User): string {
	return [u.a, u.i?.join(', '), u.ag, u.co, u.st, u.ci].filter(Boolean).join(' | ');
}

export async function whats_in_common(
	env: QEnv,
	ws: Fetcher,
	viewer_uid: string,
	a: User,
	b: User
): Promise<
	| { ok: true; text: string }
	| { ok: false; reason: 'insufficient_credits' | 'llm_error' }
> {
	const gate = await deduct(ws, viewer_uid, ESTIMATE_KOBO);
	if (!gate.ok) return { ok: false, reason: gate.reason === 'service_unavailable' ? 'llm_error' : 'insufficient_credits' };
	try {
		const text = await modal_complete(env, [
			{
				role: 'user',
				content: `In one short friendly sentence, what do these two people have in common?\nPerson A: ${profile_summary(a)}\nPerson B: ${profile_summary(b)}`
			}
		]);
		return { ok: true, text };
	} catch {
		await credit(ws, viewer_uid, ESTIMATE_KOBO);
		return { ok: false, reason: 'llm_error' };
	}
}
```
The `cost_kobo` field on the old success return (was computed from Groq's actual token usage, `pricing.ts`'s `calc_cost_usd`) has no equivalent here since `modal_complete` doesn't return usage counts — if the caller (`src/routes/api/user/[id]/common/+server.ts`) reads `r.cost_kobo` anywhere, that read must be removed too; check that route's exact body (it was reported to just do `r.ok ? { ok: true, text: r.text } : r` — if that's the full extent of its use of the result, no `cost_kobo` reference exists there and nothing else changes) before assuming it's safe to drop.

Also harden the two error paths the fork audit flagged as still-throwing rather than gracefully degrading, since "never fails" was explicit: in `src/routes/api/user/[id]/common/+server.ts`, the current `if (!viewer || !other) throw error(404, 'not found')` surfaces as a hard error page (not the graceful `commonError` UI state `findCommon()` in the client already knows how to render) when either profile genuinely has no embedding/profile yet (a very plausible case for a brand-new account, not actually exceptional) — change to return the same `{ ok: false, reason: 'llm_error' }` JSON shape the LLM-failure path already uses, so the client's existing `else commonError = body.reason ?? 'llm_error';` handles it uniformly instead of hitting an unhandled thrown 404:
```ts
export const GET: RequestHandler = async ({ params, locals }) => {
	if (!locals.user) throw error(401, 'auth');
	const viewer = (await retrieve_one(env, locals.user.id))?.payload as unknown as User | undefined;
	const other = (await retrieve_one(env, params.id))?.payload as unknown as User | undefined;
	if (!viewer || !other) return json({ ok: false, reason: 'llm_error' });
	const r = await whats_in_common(env, locals.x2_ws, locals.user.id, viewer, other);
	return json(r.ok ? { ok: true, text: r.text } : r);
};
```
